// The historical tide shape with no observable use of the list: allocate, delete, repeat. LLVM is
// entitled to erase the whole allocation on the pre-stage-1 libc path, so this is the DCE floor row,
// not a memory measurement. It is checked in to keep the before/after honest about what changed.
fn main(IOStream io) void {
    int i = 0;
    while (i < 2000000) {
        List<int> a = [1, 2, 3];
        delete a;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    io.println(i);
}
